+Fetch, follow and sync search known copies, including the last successful HTTP source and locations learned from
+verified publications, and retain the highest fully verified head sequence. Fetches run up to four locations at once,
+try each location once, and stop discovery at 64 locations with a warning. Each location has a 30-second deadline for
+its head and missing content together. Cancellation stops queued work and drains active requests.
+
+An unavailable or invalid copy does not discard a successful result. Its failure is included in the output; head
+fetch failures and verification failures are also recorded by `forum log`. A newer version can only be found if one
+of the reached copies carries it. An unchanged verified copy does not prove global freshness. Concurrent fetches,
+imports and local publishing cannot replace a stored head with an older or conflicting one.
+
+`forum sync` exits with status 2 if a followed publication cannot be fetched and verified. MCP fetch/follow/sync
+likewise mark failed operations as errors; successful fetches with failed alternatives retain their warnings.
 
