@@ -131,3 +131,11 @@
 - `forum mcp`: stdio MCP server (JSON-RPC, protocol 2025-06-18, no SDK dependency) with the same powers as the writer and CLI: list_publications, read, fetch, follow, sync, new_publication, publish (new or revision), remove, set_details, add_asset, verification_log. `--read-only` offers only the reading tools. The seed phrase is not offered over MCP.
 - Tests: `mcp` (an agent creates a publication with a custom salt, publishes, revises, reads both views; read-only mode refuses publish) and `e2e/markdown_test.go` (every view in Markdown by suffix and by Accept; HTML unchanged; no llms.txt, no robots.txt). Full suite passes. Binary smoke: `forum mcp` on the replica home returned the edited post with its parent revision.
 - GitHub: not pushed. This session has no GitHub access to Pnakotic-Codebase/forum.p2p (the API answers that the repository is not enabled for the session).
+
+## 2026-10-19: replica freshness and concurrent replication
+
+- Fixed first-valid-response selection: fetch/follow/sync retain the highest fully verified head reached, continue through failed copies, discover signed copy hints, and remember the last successful HTTP source. Equal later responses cannot erase the operation's changed status.
+- Bounded replication: four concurrent locations, 64 distinct normalized locations per fetch, 30 seconds per location across its head and missing content. Cycles are deduplicated, discovery overflow is reported, and cancellation drains started workers without starting queued locations.
+- Store.Save checks the signed head against the currently held head while holding SQLite's write lock. This closes the verification-to-save race across separate database connections and applies to network fetches, imports and local writers. Failed concurrent writes are logged as failures, not successes.
+- CLI, browser and MCP preserve partial-failure details. Unchanged copies are no longer described as globally up to date. Failed MCP fetch/follow/sync operations set isError; CLI sync returns status 2 when any followed publication cannot be refreshed. Head transport failures are included in the event log.
+- Regression coverage includes stale-first discovery, cached-source reuse, corrupt content, unavailable replicas, signed same-sequence conflicts, a slow rollback racing a newer fetch through an independent database connection, concurrency/discovery bounds, cancellation, and actual CLI/MCP output and status.
